{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 27, "model_name": "nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b", "content": "**Cherry Blossoms, Neon Lights, and Quiet Temples: My Japan Adventure**\n\nWhen I stepped off the plane in Tokyo, the city’s electric pulse greeted me instantly. Neon signs flickered over Shibuya Crossing, where a sea of umbrellas moved in synchronized rhythm despite the drizzle. I spent my first morning wandering the bustling stalls of Tsukiji Outer Market, sampling fresh tamago and steaming bowls of ramen that warmed me from the inside out.\n\nA quick train ride whisked me to Kyoto, where the pace shifted to a gentler beat. I slipped my shoes off at Kinkaku‑ji, the Golden Pavilion, and watched its reflection shimmer on the pond as cherry blossoms drifted like pink snow. Later, I joined a tea ceremony in a centuries‑old machiya house, learning the deliberate grace behind each whisked matcha sip.\n\nEvenings were for exploring hidden izakayas in Gion, where locals laughed over yakitori and shared stories of folklore. I tried my hand at making sushi in a small class, fumbling with the rice before finally rolling a decent maki that earned a nod from the chef.\n\nThe trip’s highlight came in Nara, where I fed friendly deer that bowed for crackers and wandered through Todai‑ji’s massive wooden hall, feeling the weight of history in every beam. As the sun set behind the torii gates of Fushimi Inari, thousands of vermilion pathways stretched ahead, inviting contemplation.\n\nJapan surprised me with its seamless blend of ultra‑modern vigor and timeless serenity. From the buzz of Tokyo’s streets to the quiet rustle of bamboo forests, each moment felt like a page from a living storybook—one I’ll carry home in my heart and my camera roll.", "logprobs": [{"token": "We", "logprob": -0.185306116938591}, {"token": " need", "logprob": -0.003127804258838296}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -0.0831482857465744}, {"token": " write", "logprob": -0.4172625243663788},